This is called the rogue level, as it behaves like nethack's beloved
(?) ancestor, Rogue.  Other differences include that there are no
doors, only doorways.  You must move through the doorways in one of
the NEWS directions, not on a diagonal.  All monsters created on the
level are capital letter monsters, as rogue did not use lowercase
letters or punctuation for monsters.

There is always one ghost on the level, typically named Kenneth
Arnold, Glenn Wichmann, or Michael Toy.  3 guesses as to why, and the
first 2 don't count.  The ghost will be sitting on top of a pile of
items, including:

3/4 chance of 1-7 food rations
Either a mace or two-handed sword, 50/50 split... if a mace, it will
be at +1 to +3; if a 2H sword, -1 to +3. Either has a 75% chance of
being cursed.
a +1 bow, 75% chance it is cursed
25-34 +0 arrows, 75% chance of them being cursed
Either a ring mail (+0 to +2) or plate mail (-1 to +3).  Both have a
75% chance of being cursed, and a 33% chance of being rustproof.
1/2 chance of a fake amulet of yendor.

Wizard lock and locking result in 'A dustcloud springs up in the
older, more primitive doorway.'

Monsters get no starting items when created.

As you probably noticed, there is no color on the level.

If I read mhitu.c correctly, monsters cannot use missile weapons.

Rogue level never has special rooms/shops, nor does it have fountains,
sinks, statues, or random engravings.

On rogue level, a spell/wand of light, cast/zapped in a room, will
light the entire room, not just a radius about the character.

On rogue level, there are new probabilities for each item type:  12%
weapons, 12% armor, 22% food, 22% potion, 22% scroll, 5% wand, 5%
ring.  No spellbooks, gems, tools, or amulets (other than possibly the
fake AoY in the ghost pile) are created.

Monsters don't tunnel.  I take this to mean that dwarves and rock
moles are not generated (they are not capital letters) and umber
hulks, if created, don't chew walls.  Xorns can still pass through
walls, however.

Monsters don't pick up items you use (think firing daggers at a stupid
hill orc and having it pick up each dagger as it hits him... never
moving to attack, etc.)

Scrolls of earth do nothing, as boulders are not allowed on the level.

Vision of your surroundings works somewhat different, but I don't
quite understand rogue_vision in vision.c...

In case anyone is interested in all of this, search the code for
REINCARNATION, which is the config setting that sets aside one level
of every game as a rogue level.

